{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-5-21","kind":"proposition","title":"等量关系：比例","englishTitle":"If there be three magnitudes, and others equal to them in multitude, which taken two and two together are in the same ratio, and the proportion of them be perturbed, then, if ex aequali the first magnitude is greater than the third, the fourth will also be greater than the sixth; if equal, equal; and if less, less.","book":5,"number":21,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:5.prop.21","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:5.prop.21/","group":"prop","sourceNumber":21,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-5-21@raw-209e42328a02c83f","contentId":"euclid-5-21","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"209e42328a02c83face7f4f05a4dc2e2b38d0d724c807e92e34750d787c77819","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-5-21.statement","euclid-5-21.construction.1","euclid-5-21.proof.1","euclid-5-21.proof.2","euclid-5-21.proof.3","euclid-5-21.proof.4","euclid-5-21.conclusion","euclid-5-21.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-5-21.statement","contentId":"euclid-5-21","revisionId":"euclid-5-21@raw-209e42328a02c83f","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"059c5fe5f0aa50b1d83a6087fe5024e1fdc1a7f806f2c5c9a90da99476877028","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If there be three magnitudes, and others equal to them in multitude, which taken two and two together are in the same ratio, and the proportion of them be perturbed, then, if ex aequali the first magnitude is greater than the third, the fourth will also be greater than the sixth; if equal, equal; and if less, less."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果三个等量,而其他等量,两者加在一起,比例相同,而且其中的比例也受干扰,那么,如果从平等角度讲,第一个等量大于第三个等量,第四个等量也将大于第六等;如果等量,则相等;如果差量小,则更少。"}]},{"id":"euclid-5-21.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-5-21","revisionId":"euclid-5-21@raw-209e42328a02c83f","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"58964e7d93d311aad0c12c5fc661d297254d1ceb44ca47dd703c3690ea32e166","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let there be three magnitudes A, B, C, and others D, E, F equal to them in multitude, which taken two and two are in the same ratio, and let the proportion of them be perturbed, so that, as A is to B, so is E to F, and, as B is to C, so is D to E, and let A be greater than C ex aequali; I say that D will also be greater than F; if A is equal to C, equal; and if less, less."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"330、B、C等分之3,D等分之A、E、F等分之A、E、F等分之A、A等分之A、E、C等同,两者的比例相同,因此,A至B等同E和F,B等同B等同D,A等同E,A等同大于C等分之C;我说,D等分之F也大于F;如果A等于C,则等于;如果少于A,则等于或少于C；A 与 B 之比等于 E 与 F 之比；B 与 C 之比等于 D 与 E 之比。"}]},{"id":"euclid-5-21.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-5-21","revisionId":"euclid-5-21@raw-209e42328a02c83f","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"60eb91f25e13144e46798f7a403962ca1aa76c8bbb0654a918caf047b40fdac8","citations":["euclid-5-8"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, since A is greater than C, and B is some other magnitude, therefore A has to B a greater ratio than C has to B. [[V. 8](/principles/euclid-5-8)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因为A比C,B是其他一些级,因此A必须达到Ba 较大的比比C必须达到B。 [[V. 8](/principles/euclid-5-8)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-5-21.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-5-21","revisionId":"euclid-5-21@raw-209e42328a02c83f","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"9c60ce50e059133941f059bc363bb6cfda024b7f08f741a5a353be8ffe7f6062","citations":["euclid-5-13"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But, as A is to B, so is E to F, and, as C is to B, inversely, so is E to D. Therefore also E has to F a greater ratio than E has to D. [[V. 13](/principles/euclid-5-13)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但是,A对B的比等于E对F的比,而C对B的比则等于E对D的比,因此,E对E对D的比也等于A对A对E对D的比；A 与 B 之比等于 E 与 F 之比。 [[V. 13](/principles/euclid-5-13)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-5-21.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-5-21","revisionId":"euclid-5-21@raw-209e42328a02c83f","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c1dd4bf4dd0dff201716414df9ce6c22fbde2ffc9588d079d9ed24dfdaae9c78","citations":["euclid-5-10"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But that to which the same has a greater ratio is less; [[V. 10](/principles/euclid-5-10)] therefore F is less than D; therefore D is greater than F."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但同样情况为较大的比的,则少于F的,因此,F的不到D;因此,D的大于F。 [[V. 10](/principles/euclid-5-10)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-5-21.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-5-21","revisionId":"euclid-5-21@raw-209e42328a02c83f","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"a181573af3331fda1f3fde60c264e3e8a9f10d0f3cab5ac245e0e3d6e16de695","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Similarly we can prove that, if A be equal to C, D will also be equal to F; and if less, less."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"同样,我们可以证明,如果A等于C,D等于F;如果少于F,则更少。"}]},{"id":"euclid-5-21.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-5-21","revisionId":"euclid-5-21@raw-209e42328a02c83f","order":6,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"d41f4fe56dd428c759377c807a93013dffbbe29c7596acfdac57dd182cad51b6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore etc. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,等等,证毕。"}]},{"id":"euclid-5-21.source","contentId":"euclid-5-21","revisionId":"euclid-5-21@raw-209e42328a02c83f","order":7,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"13f4d9806c737918552c38f1aedf31a8a1d9d968e19bbb40d59f49d0104915ce","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:5.prop.21/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:5.prop.21\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-5-21:euclid-5-8:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-5-21","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-5-21.proof.1"],"targetContentId":"euclid-5-8","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:5.prop.21","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:5.prop.21/","sourceLabel":"V. 8"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-5-21:euclid-5-13:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-5-21","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-5-21.proof.2"],"targetContentId":"euclid-5-13","type":"depends_on","